7b4a1bd054ef486148610e518b1be05cfc), tree `c10faac2d156cac06f9f803d63f50d15e3ca82bf`. The 17-file update preserves the intervening owner commits through `e0d3ae24` and addresses the demonstrated workspace timestamp defect and both published review findings.\n\n- Workspace receipt and request observations now use the actual captured acceptance time as their common monotonic origin. Absolute deadlines, current-policy authority and independent full-startup timing remain unchanged. The separate 100-workspace readiness failures still require evidence and repair.\n- The public scanner function loads on first access, preserving the actual function, model exports, discovery, concurrent access and reload behavior. Scanning import side effects move to first scanner access; the function is absent from the raw package dictionary until then.\n- Supplemental launcher failures retain finite evidence from the already-returned process result, while preserving the original route assertion and unknown child attribution. Default-auto failure reports retain existing finite writer failure maps without an additional snapshot, request or wait.\n- The paired test fixture uses the current corpus-identity producer with an explicit synthetic scope and unqualified reference status. Strict report admission and insufficient-sample rejection remain. Pi discovery and workspace phase selection use explicit conditionals with the same evaluation order.\n- Earlier native receipt bindings, atomic approval consumption, Windows storage admission, narrowly bounded macOS socket recovery, worker-test failure propagation and reviewed partitions remain in place. The stopped F campaign stays immutable and inactive.\n\n| Evidence scope | Result and limitation |\n| --- | --- |\n| Current source, local combined validation | 561 Python tests passed with two existing skips across 31 modules. All 19 observed files remained unchanged during execution. Ruff, formatting and diff checks passed. The 18-file focused type check reported zero errors and 1,212 warnings. |\n| Broader local type diagnostic | The expanded 19-file check reports ten errors and 1,255 warnings in two unchanged publisher test functions. An actual baseline check reproduces the same ten errors. This result is retained separately from the configured production type gate, which analyzes `src`. |\n| Current source, hosted CI | Fresh checks are running on `8f15b37b`; predecessor results do not supply current-source acceptance. No Rust production file changed in this 17-file update. |\n| Predecessor `e0d3ae24`, normal installed validation | All four native jobs completed successfully before this PR advance. Windows passed 13 storage controls; each Mac passed 22 client controls and all 14 normal SLO gates. Each of those three platforms recorded 21 native decisions and 21 committed receipts with zero failure/drop/pending. Sonar analysis and its guard passed at that revision. The three-file predecessor delta does not explain the earlier intermittent Windows and Intel failures. |\n| Closed `017f1244` cohort | Linux completed 100,000 requests and 250,000 receipts with zero request/health failures, one stable resident and 3.2143% RSS growth. The complete normal census retained six failures. The observer completed 600 hooks and 605 receipts, but incomplete resource coverage, 13.8585% RSS growth above its 12% gate, and workspace failures kept it unqualified. All failed reports remain preserved. |\n| Isolated lazy-export diagnostic | The separately bound pure two-file child completed one fixed-order ARM block per artifact, 88 calls each. Candidate serial and concurrency-16 timings still miss the original 50/100/200 ms limits. This small instrumented comparison neither replaces the original baseline nor demonstrates qualified benefit. |\n| Review | Both demonstrated P1/P2 findings are fixed on the published source, with replies linking their validation. All 57 threads were verified resolved after those replies. A fresh review of this head and genuine independent last-push/CODEOWNER approval remain required. |\n\nThe original comparison baseline remains `2e672d2d950c6ec471005ddba46e49bba16dc23b`. Installed paired and observer records preserve setup, semantic, timing, resource and rollback failures at their actual boundaries. Compatible-prior rollback success does not establish original-baseline rollback, candidate restoration, signing or live release qualification. Normal smoke success does not satisfy the full PRD's workloads, sampling or performance targets.\n\nThe [original PRD, TODO, Takeaway and ledger](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/tree/75bb8692b5eaaf6f2e138d5da20402b7d270a9bb/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion/originals) preserve all 144 task objects and 119 catalog entries. The [published closed `2433a8` checkpoint](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/tree/3d9ff3ba27939b4a3e227208c8ce0f8ab8e49e15/review-evidence/2026-09-19/pr2974-completion/addenda/20260920T033147Z-2433a8-closed) contains 285 verified files. The next PRD, full TODO and Takeaway continuation packet is undergoing final preservation and reference checks; it promotes no archived task status and keeps each source cohort separate.\n\nRelevant completed runs: [predecessor normal native validation](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/actions/runs/35489693381), [closed `017f` observer](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/actions/runs/35487350949), [closed `017f` paired validation](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/actions/runs/35487350928), and [isolated lazy-export diagnostic](https://github.com/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/actions/runs/35491009774).\n\nRelease acceptance remains open: terminal current-source checks, full installed platform and performance qualification, the remaining file-size review scope, signing/update/rollback/canary proof, the configured Greptile threshold, and eligible independent last-push/CODEOWNER approval. Original sampling, latency, resource, benefit, authority and containment criteria remain unchanged. This PR does not establish complete implementation, qualification, approval, activation or release.\n","created_at":"2026-09-17T17:49:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-20T05:22:44Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"edb59c485cee40db45bb56cb0bb327f47a3254a6","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"deep-purple-boots","id":301892678,"node_id":"U_kgDOEf6ERg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301892678?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots","html_url":"https://github.com/deep-purple-boots","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deep-purple-boots/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/pulls/2974/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/pulls/2974/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/issues/2974/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hashgraph-online/hol-guard/statuses/8f15b37b4a1bd054ef486148610e518b1be05cfc","he